{"url": "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/applying/application-fee-and-waivers/", "final_url": "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/applying/application-fee-and-payment/", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-30", "text": "Skip to main content\nProspective Students\nNew and Current Students\nPostdoctoral Fellows\nFaculty and Staff\nAlumni\nSupport Rackham\nSearch\nPrograms of Study\nAdmissions\nFunding\nNavigating Your Degree\nProfessional Development\nStudent Experience\nAbout\nHome\nAdmissions\nApplying\nApplication Fee and Payment\nApplication Fee and Payment\nThe application fee is due when you submit your application. The fee is non-refundable and subject to change. If you pay the application fee and you are later approved to receive a fee waiver, the fee will not be refunded.\nUnited States citizens and those with permanent resident visa status: $75\nNon-U.S. citizens: $90\nCurrent Rackham student (regardless of citizenship): $10\nRackham Application Fee Waiver Program\nGoal\nThe purpose of the graduate application fee waiver program administered by Rackham is to lower the financial barrier for potential applicants to Rackham master\u2019s and doctoral programs. In this way, we support Rackham\u2019s goal of increasing access to graduate education.\nEligibility for a Rackham Application Fee Waiver\nAt this time, Rackham application fee waivers are available for U.S. citizens and permanent residents who have demonstrated financial need. Financial need is demonstrated by having been the recipient of a Pell grant and/or by having a Student Aid Index (SAI) of <$1,500.\nHow to Apply for a Rackham Application Fee Waiver\nTo apply for a fee waiver, a prospective applicant should complete the fee waiver request within the Rackham graduate application and upload their Student Aid Index (SAI) from their Federal Application of Federal Student Aid (FAFSA); the SAI must be less than $1,500 for the applicant to be eligible. Alternatively, if a prospective applicant is not currently enrolled in an undergraduate or graduate program, they may establish their financial need through demonstrated Pell Grant eligibility, documentation for which can be found in the FAFSA assessment or financial aid letter from the most recent institution. This process must be completed prior to submission of the graduate application; no refunds can be provided once a graduate application is submitted.\nOther Sources of Application Fee Waivers\nThere are other sources of application fee waivers outside of this Rackham-administered program. Within the university, individual Rackham graduate programs may have their own fee waiver programs; prospective applicants should reach out to their intended program directly to inquire prior to submitting an application. In addition, if a prospective applicant participated in research or graduate school preparatory programs at the University of Michigan, they may be eligible for a fee waiver from those programs. These include programs such as the U-M Student Research Opportunity Program (SROP), Michigan Humanities Emerging Research Scholars Program(MICHHERS) and Bridges to the Doctorate programs; participants in those programs should contact the programs directly to obtain a fee waiver code. Receipt of a fee waiver from either an individual Rackham graduate program or a Rackham preparatory program is governed by applicable state and federal law, as well as university policy.\nContact Admissions\nHours: Admissions is open Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. The office is closed Saturdays and Sundays and on university holidays.\nLocation\n0120 Rackham Building\n915 East Washington Street\nAnn Arbor, MI 48109-1070\nContact\nPhone: 734.764.8129\nFax: 734.936.3335\nEmail: rackadmis@umich.edu\n915 East Washington Street\nAnn Arbor, MI 48109 USA\n734.764.4400\nContact Us\nSupport Rackham\nSitemap\nPrograms of Study\nAdmissions\nFunding\nNavigating Your Degree\nProfessional Development\nStudent Experience\nAbout\nAudiences\nProspective Students\nNew and Current Students\nPostdoctoral Fellows\nFaculty and Staff\nAlumni\nSocial Media\nBluesky\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nYouTube\n\u00a9 2026 The Regents of the University of Michigan\nProduced by Michigan Creative, a unit of the Office of the Vice President for Communications\nBack to Top", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/applying/application-fee-and-payment/#main"], ["", "https://rackham.umich.edu/"], ["", "https://rackham.umich.edu/"], ["Prospective Students", "https://rackham.umich.edu/prospective-students/"], ["New and Current Students", "https://rackham.umich.edu/current-students/"], ["Postdoctoral Fellows", "https://postdocs.umich.edu/"], ["Faculty and Staff", "https://rackham.umich.edu/faculty-and-staff/"], ["Alumni", "https://rackham.umich.edu/alumni/"], ["Support Rackham", "https://rackham.umich.edu/support-rackham/"], ["", "https://rackham.umich.edu/"], ["Programs of Study", "https://rackham.umich.edu/programs-of-study/"], ["Programs of Study", "https://rackham.umich.edu/programs-of-study/"], ["Certificate Programs", "https://rackham.umich.edu/programs-of-study/certificate-programs/"], ["Dual Degree Programs", "https://rackham.umich.edu/programs-of-study/dual-degree-programs/"], ["Graduate and Professional Degree Programs Not Administered by Rackham", "https://rackham.umich.edu/programs-of-study/non-rackham-programs/"], ["Admissions", "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/"], ["Campus Applications", "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/#campus-applications"], ["Ann Arbor", "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/applying/"], ["Dearborn", "https://umdearborn.edu/academics/graduate-studies"], ["Flint", "https://www.umflint.edu/graduateprograms/apply.htm"], ["Applying", "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/applying/"], ["Considering Graduate School", "https://rackham.umich.edu/admissions/applying/#considering"], ["Preparing Your Application", "https://rackham.u